#: ../../source/guides/index.md:48
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The first three of those happen in **different repositories** — a formats"
" repository and an input database are maintained separately from the "
"engine, by whoever wants to. That is the same decision twice: coverage "
"should grow without anybody touching the part that must not change. "
"{doc}`../overview/the-repositories` is the map."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/index.md:53
msgid "The three kinds of page you will meet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/index.md:54
msgid ""
"**A guide page** tells you how to do something, in order, in the "
"repository you are in. It is the kind of page you are reading now."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/index.md:57
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**A reference page** answers \"what does this option do\" for every "
"option, without caring who is asking. It lives under "
"{doc}`../reference/index` and is linked from every guide that needs it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/index.md:60
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**A generated page** is written by a command, not by a person — the two "
"API references, the coverage of the grants, the last gate run. It lives "
"under {doc}`../generated/index`, and every one of them says which command"
" to run to check it yourself."
msgstr ""

